      simpleExplanation: "People naturally want protection against life's risks, and Islam doesn't reject that instinct - the Prophet himself told a man to tie up his camel before trusting in God. Muslims avoided conventional insurance partly because of a mistaken belief that any insurance questions God's will (a myth) and partly because conventional insurance genuinely involves Riba, Gharar and gambling (a real problem) - so scholars developed Takaful to meet the real need without the real problem.",
